[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3815475501","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3815475501","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":3815475501,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ja4kt","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T04:50:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T05:03:06Z","body":"I don't have a C# environment, so I can't see the MRP (If possible, please upload the GDScript project), but I think I can answer a few things.\n\nRegarding the issue of particular slowdowns during playback, I believe there has long been concern that string searches during path finding for the Node object and their properties from SceneTree when generating the blend cache are slow. And the performance at this stage depends on the number of animations because it caches the union of all tracks held by every animation for blending (crossfading or deterministic = write default behavior in the case of AnimationPlayer).\n\nSo, finding ways to speed this up is likely not straightforward. However, to reduce performance hitch on playback, we could consider changing the timing of cache generation, similar to asynchronous loading. For example, searching for objects from trackpaths can be handled when adding scenes or manually, and generating indexes for union sets can be handled on the AnimationLibrary resource side, not the AnimationMixerNode.\n\nRegarding other matters, there was an issue with slow memory allocation and iteration for dynamic arrays. Several pull requests are currently being worked on to address this. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112308","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3815475501/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824980665","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3824980665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":3824980665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j_JK5","user":{"login":"Avantir-Chaosfire","id":11003232,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDAzMjMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11003232?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire","html_url":"https://github.com/Avantir-Chaosfire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T18:04:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T18:04:33Z","body":"@TokageItLab I'll take a look at putting together a GDScript version. But it seems strange to me that you're talking about the speed of caching, when the numbers I'm complaining about happen every single time an animation runs, not just the first time. Is caching happening on every call to AnimationPlayer.Play()?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824980665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825635801","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3825635801","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":3825635801,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kBpHZ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T20:37:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T20:44:06Z","body":"Yes. When AnimationPlayer is stopped, the track cache is cleared, and calling play() will search the scene tree and iterate through all animations again. BTW, if you play the next animation without stopping current animation, re-caching will not occur.\nSo clearing cache does not occur as long as it's not stopped and there are no changes to the AnimationLibrary, but an option to let the user decide how long to maintain the cache and create cache manually (such as on load scene) might be considerable. It might reduce performance hitches when call play() as mentioned above.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3825635801/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827064288","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3827064288","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":3827064288,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kHF3g","user":{"login":"Avantir-Chaosfire","id":11003232,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDAzMjMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11003232?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire","html_url":"https://github.com/Avantir-Chaosfire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T01:16:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T01:16:19Z","body":"Yeah that sounds like a good idea. But I also just got it working in GDScript (assuming I didn't make any mistakes converting it) and it doesn't seem to have the problem at all:\n\n[AnimationPlayerPerformanceMRPNoCSharp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24976282/AnimationPlayerPerformanceMRPNoCSharp.zip)\n\nThe numbers are literally 10x smaller, often under 100 microseconds to play an animation, and 10-40 to play an ongoing animation.\n\nSo it seems like some aspect of the C# wrapper here is making this very, very inefficient","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3827064288/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828710902","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3828710902","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":3828710902,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kNX32","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T15:26:02Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T15:26:02Z","body":"If it's a C#-specific issue, it might be related to something affecting the search for the animation name or segment to play. Since I'm not very familiar with C#, this is just a guess, but could it be related to the fact that play() internally takes many arguments? cc @raulsntos ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828710902/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828772523","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3828772523","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":3828772523,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kNm6r","user":{"login":"Avantir-Chaosfire","id":11003232,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDAzMjMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11003232?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire","html_url":"https://github.com/Avantir-Chaosfire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Avantir-Chaosfire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T16:12:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T16:12:52Z","body":"It seems very weird to me that it appears to be C# specific - because from my testing the performance scales both with the number of tracks on the animation being played and the number of animations on the animation player, both of which should have no part in the C# wrapper...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3828772523/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3829390733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-3829390733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":3829390733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kP92N","user":{"login":"Ryan-000","id":73148864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTQ4ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73148864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000","html_url":"https://github.com/Ryan-000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryan-000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-31T21:31:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T21:31:37Z","body":"IIRC, when I was profiling this in my project, it mostly came down to the C# layer being very inefficient for property get/set, which is expected for the amount of indirection. This applied outside of Animation as well, I saw the same behaviour in `MultiplayerSynchronizer`.\n\nIn your actual project, check `SetGodotClassPropertyValue` in `_ScriptProperties.generated.cs`. Since every Variant-compatible member is added to that, the method becomes slower in larger classes, especially when setting a native base-class property (like `position` on `Node3D`), since it checks subclasses first before falling back to the base.\n\nIn 4.5, there was an issue where attaching a C# script to `AnimationPlayer`/`AnimationTree` caused `_post_process_key_value` to jump to C# on every call even when no override existed. So I had to avoid attaching C# scripts on those nodes to improve performance.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3829390733/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5901708226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115550#issuecomment-5901708226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115550","id":5901708226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABX8Trwg","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T00:33:45Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T00:33:45Z","body":"If the problem was the `SetGodotClassPropertyValue` in `_ScriptProperties.generated.cs`, then that should be fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116300 which now generates trampolines with direct access instead of a long list of if-else conditions.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5901708226/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]